od the high streets not  happened  absolutely no and i think that was a lot  of the hope um and part of that is just  people thinking about some of the  challenges in terms of uncertainty as  rachel says around the future and  obviously the higher costs of inflation  beginning to bite and energy bills don't  forget we are in  um april the weather's been quite lovely  but but come the autumn even the  existing energy price even if it doesn't  go up any higher and not many people  think that that's going to be the case  the the bills that people might be  looking at coming into the autumn will  be very difficult indeed and so i quite  understand why consumers are not  splashing the cash and are continuing um  to tighten their belts in anticipation  of things becoming more difficult but  obviously then you're in a spiral um  where that lack of consumer confidence  and that lack of spending serves to  dampen business confidence anita and  rachel thank you both

